n['review'](r,p,'Full339-line guide and all exact block occurrences read. Runnable/valid eval preconditions and same-call trace/grade/usage; model/config propagation through subagents; stochastic build variance separate from scorer reps; explicit optimization target and non-regression constraints, scope/offlimits/check-in/spend contract; harness path hash is change detector, command allowlist not hash described as execution boundary; durable per-round snapshots, random stratified fixed split and withheld analyzer inputs; frozen env fingerprints and contemporaneous unchanged controls; one hypothesis across multiple hunks, predicted recoveries and regressions, trace-cited changes; API acceptance/resolvedscope/canary before expensive full pass; completeness before reporting, costs from all billed attempts; newmetrics regrade all variants, suspiciousjudge/engagement indicators distinct; stall taxonomy and breadth coverage with attribution tradeoff; finaltest if truly withheld and required-versus-tuning edits. Declared source train/test isolation is instruction-based handoff, not a structural access guarantee; baseline-failure review occurs before split and can contaminate later withheld cases; default so-called test selects winner each round, so it is validation. Reps do not remove shared-build dependence. Every CI/count/plateau/example efficacy/model/cost/budget heuristic is unverified; interval overlap is not a substitute for a paired effect analysis, unchanged engagement does not prove no quality effect, and flat-score diagnoses are hypotheses. Scrubbing short zero outcomes can conceal real no-op failures; preserve raw/excluded totals and fixed predicates. Runner/report behavior still pending implementation review.',[k1,k2,k3,'core-anthro-build-score-variance','core-anthro-heldout-channel','core-anthro-attempt-result-coherence','core-addy-activation-not-outcome'])
row=next(x for rr in n['DATA']['repositories'] if rr['repo']==r for x in rr['coverage'] if x['path']==p);row['exact_block_review']={'ledger':'core-anthro-api-blocks.json','unique_block_ids':sorted(ids),'all_occurrences_closed':True}
rr=next(x for x in n['DATA']['repositories'] if x['repo']==r);rr['source_flaw_evidence'].append({'claim':'Hillclimb default uses its named test set every round to select the best variant, so that set is validation. Passing only train paths to an analyzer is a prompt-level restriction; the guide does not provide a structural access boundary, and baseline failure review occurs before the split.','sources':[src(r,p,35,39,'Baseline-failure review'),src(r,p,205,215,'Default split and selection'),src(r,p,225,239,'Analyzer handoff and claimed isolation')]})
